 "Vračar, Golsvortijeva 21": "Vračar, Golsvortijeva 21",
 "Ručno rađene kožne torbe, sandale, papuče i kaiševi, tunižanska keramika i tadžini, ćilimi, nakit i nargile. Maloprodaja i veleprodaja.": "Handmade leather bags, sandals, slippers and belts, Tunisian ceramics and tagines, rugs, jewellery and hookahs. Retail and wholesale.",
 "Jamila, prirodna nega sa shea puterom": "Jamila, natural care with shea butter",
 "Online": "Online",
 "Radi i afričke ručne lepeze.": "She also makes handmade African fans.",
 "Istorija muslimana Beograda duga je više vekova. Od 1521. godine i uspostavljanja osmanske vlasti, Beograd se razvijao u jedan od značajnih urbanih, trgovačkih i kulturnih centara Osmanskog carstva na evropskom tlu. Brojne džamije, medrese, tekije, hamami, čaršije i vakufi činili su neraskidivi deo njegovog urbanog i društvenog života.": "The history of Belgrade's Muslims spans many centuries. From 1521 and the establishment of Ottoman rule, Belgrade grew into one of the major urban, trade and cultural centres of the Ottoman Empire on European soil. Numerous mosques, madrasas, tekkes, hammams, bazaars and waqfs were an inseparable part of its urban and social life.",
 "Devetnaesti vek doneo je dramatične promene – prisilno iseljavanje muslimanskog stanovništva i nestajanje najvećeg dela islamskog vizuelnog i arhitektonskog nasleđa Beograda. Ipak, muslimanski život u Beogradu nije ugašen. Obnova Bajrakli džamije 1868. godine i zvanično priznanje islamske veroispovesti u Kneževini Srbiji označili su početak novog poglavlja u istoriji zajednice.": "The nineteenth century brought dramatic change – the forced emigration of the Muslim population and the disappearance of most of Belgrade's Islamic visual and architectural heritage. Yet Muslim life in Belgrade was not extinguished. The restoration of the Bajrakli Mosque in 1868 and the official recognition of the Islamic faith in the Principality of Serbia marked the beginning of a new chapter in the community's history.",
 "Tokom Kraljevine, a potom i socijalističke Jugoslavije, muslimanska zajednica se obnavljala i rasla, obogaćena dolaskom muslimana iz različitih krajeva zemlje i sveta. Uprkos izazovima koji su pratili raspad Jugoslavije i decenije koje su usledile, muslimani su nastavili da grade svoj život u Beogradu.": "During the Kingdom and later socialist Yugoslavia, the Muslim community renewed itself and grew, enriched by Muslims arriving from different parts of the country and the world. Despite the challenges that came with the breakup of Yugoslavia and the decades that followed, Muslims continued to build their lives in Belgrade.",
 "Danas muslimansko prisustvo u Beogradu ponovo dobija na vitalnosti. Novi džemati i sve raznovrsniji društveni i kulturni život svedoče o snazi zajednice i njenom potencijalu.": "Today the Muslim presence in Belgrade is gaining vitality again. New communities and an increasingly diverse social and cultural life bear witness to the community's strength and its potential.",
 "Upravo u toj dubokoj ukorenjenosti i postojanosti prepoznajemo duh istrajnosti koji je vekovima oblikovao muslimansko prisustvo u Beogradu i koji danas predstavlja temelj za izgradnju budućnosti zajednice u našem gradu.": "It is precisely in this deep rootedness and steadfastness that we recognise the spirit of perseverance that has shaped the Muslim presence in Belgrade for centuries, and which today is the foundation for building the community's future in our city.",
 "Pročitaj više": "Read more",
